# =============================================================================
#  MMC-MAC.orch - Multimodal Access Control
#  Workflow Description Language, AIF V3.0
#
#  The User Agent never addresses a Module: it asks the Controller. See
#  HCI-MAD.orch for the mapping of each request onto the Controller API.
#
#  The user presents a face and a passphrase; the Module matches both against
#  the Subject Gallery that MMC-ACR wrote and renders its verdict.
#
#  PENDING - THE VERDICT IS NOT AT THE BOUNDARY. 1MMC-MAC-V2.5-I01 today declares
#  Response, VocalResponse and FaceDescriptors: the verdict rendered in words
#  and in a face, and not the verdict itself. A User Agent therefore cannot
#  learn whether the person was admitted; it can only play a recording of the
#  avatar saying so, and a User Agent that must read meaning from an utterance
#  cannot be generated from Metadata.
#
#  OSD-IDR-V1.5 now emits Identification, a Boolean, beside UserID. MMC-MAC
#  should carry both to its own boundary. The branch below is written as it will
#  read once it does, and marked so that it is not mistaken for something the
#  current Metadata supports.
# =============================================================================

workflow MMC-MAC over 1MMC-MAC-V2.5-I01

on Start:
    ask Controller to start 1MMC-MAC-V2.5-I01

    prompt  "Welcome to the HCI Multimodal Access Control Service.
             Look at the camera."
    wait    1s
    acquire UserFace (OSD-BVO-V1.5)

    prompt  "Speak your passphrase."
    acquire UserSpeech (OSD-BSO-V1.5) via VAD

    ask Controller to take UserFace   (OSD-BVO-V1.5) for 1MMC-MAC-V2.5-I01
    ask Controller to take UserSpeech (OSD-BSO-V1.5) for 1MMC-MAC-V2.5-I01

    ask Controller to give from 1MMC-MAC-V2.5-I01:
        Identification (Boolean),                 # PENDING: not yet declared
        UserID         (OSD-IID-V1.5),            # PENDING: not yet declared
        VocalResponse  (OSD-BSO-V1.5),
        MachineFace    (PAF-FDO-V1.6)

    branch on Identification {
        present VocalResponse, MachineFace
        display "{UserID}, welcome."
    } else {
        present VocalResponse, MachineFace
        display "You have not been identified."
    }

on Stop:
    ask Controller to stop 1MMC-MAC-V2.5-I01
